sentences.t:
Otro día mañana métense a andar,
a qual dizen Medina ivan albergar,
e de Medina a Molina en otro día van;

sentences.l:
Other day morning they-put-themselves to travel,
to which they-call Medina they-went to-lodge,
and from Medina to Molina in another day they-go;

sentences.t:
Al que en buen ora nasco llegava el menssaje,
privado cavalga, a reçebirlos sale;
armas iva teniendo e grant gozo que faze.

sentences.l:
To-him who in good hour was-born was-arriving the message,
quickly he-rides, to receive-them he-goes-out;
arms he-was-going holding and great joy that he-makes.

sentences.t:
Besaron las manos las fijas al padre.
Teniendo ivan armas, entráronse a la cibdad;
grand gozo fizo con ellas doña Ximena su madre.

sentences.l:
Kissed the hands the daughters to-the father.
Holding they-were-going arms, they-entered-themselves to the city;
great joy made with them doña Ximena their mother.

He married my daughters, for not them-to-them gave I;
since them they-have left to great dishonour,
if dishonour there fits any against us,
the little and the great all is of my lord.

sentences.t:
Assí commo entraron por medio de la cort,
ví[d]olos el rey e coñosció a Muño Gustioz;
levantós el rey tan bien los reçibió.

sentences.l:
As-soon-as they-entered through middle of the court,
saw-them the king and recognized Muño Gustioz;
rose-himself the king so well them he-received.

sentences.t:
“Merçed, rey, de largos reynos a vos dizen señor!
Los pie[de]s e las manos vos besa el Campeador;
elle es vuestro vassallo e vos sodes so señor.

sentences.l:
“Mercy, king, of wide kingdoms to you they-call lord!
The feet and the hands to-you kisses the Campeador;
he is your vassal and you are his lord.

sentences.t:
Ya vos sabedes la ondra que es cuntida a nos,
qu[o]mo nos han abiltados infantes de Carrión:
mal majaron sus fijas del Çid Campeador;

sentences.l:
Now you know the honour that has befallen to us,
how us have debased Infantes of Carrión:
badly they-beat his daughters of-the Çid Campeador;

sentences.t:
Por esto vos besa las manos, commo vassallo a señor,
que gelos levedes a vistas, o a juntas o a cortes;
tienes por desondrado, mas la vuestra es mayor,

sentences.l:
For this to-you he-kisses the hands, as vassal to lord,
that them-to-him you-may-bring to meeting, or to assemblies or to courts;
he-holds-himself for dishonoured, but the yours is greater,

sentences.t:
“Verdad te digo yo, que me pesa de coraçón,
e verdad dizes en esto, tú, Muño Gustioz,
ca yo casé sus fijas con ifantes de Carrión;

sentences.l:
“Truth to-you tell I, that me it-grieves from heart,
and truth you-say in this, you, Muño Gustioz,
for I married his daughters with Infantes of Carrión;

What not I-was-thinking to-do in all this season,
will-go my officers through all [the] kingdom mine,
for within in Toledo they-will-proclaim my court,
that there to-me may-go counts and lesser-nobles;
